    "intro_narrative": "You awaken in the belly of an enormous airship, the steady thrum of its steam engines vibrating through the metal grates beneath your boots. The air is thick with the scent of ozone, coal smoke, and machine oil. Surrounding you is a complex network of brass pipes, ticking clockwork mechanisms, and hissing valves. This is the fabled Aether-Leviathan, a masterpiece of steampunk engineering that has mysteriously gone off course. The main hatch is sealed by heavy blast doors, and the only way to escape before the boiler pressure overloads the hull is to re-activate the Master Transmitter. However, the ship's intricate mechanical logic systems have scattered the activation sequence across multiple interconnected devices. You must carefully trace the flow of steam, gears, and aetheric energy from one apparatus to the next, operating them in the correct sequence to override the lockdown and send out an SOS.",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
  },
